\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Identity loops and noncommuting loops}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{At #{U=V=1} in the [one-vertex model](fdip-00ZA),
both pullbacks are the identity. Hence
#{\extD_{1,1}=0} and #{\det K_{1,1}(m)=m^{16}}.
The 4 cell slots remain present even though all
uncoupled cellular differences vanish.}

\p{At #{U=\qi}, #{V=\qj}, the pullbacks are
#{L_{-\qi}} and #{L_{-\qj}}. Their products are
#{T_1T_2=L_{\qk}} and #{T_2T_1=L_{-\qk}}, as in
\ref{fdip-00SN}. The cochain differential therefore
retains noncommuting paths on the same 4 slots.}
